  delete_route(destination) — Delete a route from the routing table.
    - destination: Destination network in CIDR notation, e.g. '10.0.12.0/30'
  ping(target_ip, [count]) — Send ICMP echo requests to test reachability of an IP address.
    - target_ip: Target IP address
    - count (optional): Number of packets to send (default 3)
  report_done(message, success) — Signal that you want to terminate and are satisfied with the current state of the entire network. Can only be issued alone without any other tool calls in the same response. 
    - message: Summary of routes added and connectivity verified
    - success: True if full connectivity was achieved
  send_message(to, message) — Send a natural language message to another node's agent. The message will be injected into the recipient's context on its next iteration.
    - to: Name of the destination node, e.g. 'h2'
    - message: The message to send
  wait([timeout]) — Block until a message arrives from another node (or until timeout). Use this when you have completed your local actions and need to wait for other nodes to respond or coordinate before proceeding.
    - timeout (optional): Maximum seconds to wait for a message (default: 5)

